# This repository is LF-only, in the working copy as well as in the object store.
#
# Not a style preference. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows clone would check out
# scripts/validate-repo.sh with CRLF line endings, and a shell script whose lines
# end in \r fails in ways that read as a broken gate rather than a broken
# checkout. The generated harness has the same property enforced at a different
# layer: render_harness.py writes LF regardless of platform and
# validate_harness.py rejects a package containing CRLF, so a package rendered on
# Windows is byte-identical to one rendered on Linux.
#
# Keeping the checkout LF too means the plugin scripts a repository installs are
# byte-identical to the plugin scripts under test, which is exactly what the
# validator's session-tooling hash check compares.

* text=auto eol=lf
